                <pb facs="0256" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2014: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-09T14:00:00-05:00">October 9, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>70. Your 163, October 8, 9 a.m.,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d153-f1"/> Inform Drummond
                    that I trust that he intends to advise calling the meeting of the Council.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
